<title>FRANCE: GEC ALSTHOM WINS 1.3 BLN FFR ELECTRIC PLANT ORDER.</title>
<headline>GEC ALSTHOM WINS 1.3 BLN FFR ELECTRIC PLANT ORDER.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Franco-British engineering group GEC Alsthom said on Wednesday that it had won a 1.3 billion franc ($205 million) order to build the largest electric plant in Chile.</p>
<p>As part of an order by Nordeste Pacifico Energia Limitada, a company created by Chilean electricity producer Endesa and U.S. company CMS Energy, GEC Alsthom will build the 740 megawatt Atacama plant near Mejillones in northern Chile.</p>
<p>The plant will enter service in the first quarter of 1999, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452 ($ = 6.340 French Francs)</p>
</text>
